From&nbsp;<a href="http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/multiverse/heroes/the-scholar">http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/multiverse/heroes/the-scholar</a> in the Scholar of the Infinite bio
<div class="bb-quote">Quote:<br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">John Rhodes has learned far too much and seen too deeply. His disconnection from time and reality has given him an ideal position to provide support for those who can make a difference in the coming upheaval, but  recent powerful adversaries have targeted the very ley-lines that bind The Scholar&rsquo;s form to this plane. 
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
Deadline had some impact I&#39;m sure but I don&#39;t think it was just him. &nbsp;A related hint is that the unlock conditions for Scholar of the Infinite in e video game dealt with Scholar being incapped in a win against Apostate or Gloomweaver after he did some healing. &nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Do you think someone might have been targeting them specifically to cause an end to the Scholar? Perhaps trying to get him out of the way before the final battle?

[quote="Foote"]

Finally I can talk about stuff!!!!&nbsp;Ok. Where to start.....Writhe was talked about a bit in this thread. <a href="https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/footenotes-writhe-the-belltower-and-setback-4686" rel="nofollow">I had a theory about Writhe from the moment we saw him in the V5 expansion which you can read here</a>. It seems that I was pretty spot on, at least the new artwork supports my view more than refutes it. The Spiderman-Setback/Writhe-Venom correlation is so strong in the artwork. Look out for the &quot;Cloak&quot; to be a possible villain candidate moving forward.I think it will be no surprise that one of the most facinating loose storylines coming out of the new artwork pertains to Scholar and Guise. Scholar&#39;s promo incap suggests to me a strong connection between them since they are both fading/melting away together at the same time. This combined with a non-trivial amount of other artwork showing them together really ticks my interest meter. I&#39;m sure the connection between them lays within &quot;ley-lines&quot;. Guise is the opposite coin face of Wager Master, <a href="https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/footenotes-chaos-vs-order-and-the-crisis-of-the-multiverse-6527" rel="nofollow">who himself maybe the opposite coin face of our big bad cosmic entity</a>. With Scholar and his stone being a possible &quot;gateway&quot; &nbsp;between our world and the cosmic entity (as hinted at in his bio), there is more at play here than we know. This is a hero pairing to keep a close eye on in the final expansion.Let&#39;s talk about <strong>Ammit</strong>!
<blockquote>If this is the path you choose, your form will be bound to this plane, but your spirit will fade-Ammit, Ra: Horus of Two Horizons
&nbsp;
</blockquote>
The innitial thought here is that Ammit is more than likely talking to Ra right? There seems to be some sort of deal being made where Ra would get more powerful in order to go back and defeat the Ennead at the cost of his spirit. Given the comic this comes from, it makes a ton of sense as something thats possible. Given the backstory to &quot;beard Ra&quot;, this would neatly explain his long absence as well as his more powered-up glorious return to kick some major egyptian ass. This looks pretty cut-and-dry here.But I&#39;d like to pose an alternate theory. What if he is not talking to Ra, but to <em>Nightmist</em> instead? Consider the following:Form bound to a plane without a spirit. That could be said of Ra, as going forward in Tactics, we see the form of Ra but as a different person for all accounts. But we see the same thing with Nightmist in Tactics as well. Her mistform is bound to this plane, but she as a person/consiousness is no where to be found and considered lost/dead.In the Tomb of Anubis deck, The Staff of Anubis has flavor texts suggesting that she has weilded the staff and felt its power. It&#39;s a strong connection to Ra&#39;s story and to the Underworld where Ammit is from.&nbsp;It has not been talked about too much, but Dark Watch Nightmist clearly has Egyptian infuences with the markings under her eyes. Nothing about it is in her backstory, but the art decision is likely not arbitrary.&nbsp;<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Ammit is marked as a nemesis to Ra. A nemesis. Why would there be a deal here, why would Ammit allow a nemesis some support even if it comes as a sizable cost? It&#39;s possible sure, but the interaction doesn&#39;t sound as one between enemies. Another possible point for this conversation being with someone other than Ra? This is a far weaker point than the others, but it&#39;s somethign I thought worth considering.A lot of this depends on timing, and we don&#39;t know 100% when the Horus storyline takes place in the grand scheme of things. We also know that Ra is also saved by Fanatic at some point in the &quot;Trial by Fire&quot; one-shot comic, but again, when that takes place exactly is nearly impossible to tell (though from the art I would guess Fanatic saves him post bearded transformation). Is it possible that Nightmist has a significant hand in Ra&#39;s ascention to Horus, going so far as to give up her spirit to save/help Ra?&nbsp;How cool is the card&nbsp;Quando? Ahora! ?!?! Not really much to say here that hasn&#39;t been said. But the brief look into an alternate universe and far different story paths for familiar heros/villains is pretty fugg&#39;in cool.How cool is Hammer/Anvil&#39;s incap art?! We knew from bio&#39;s that Dark Visionary went well past the acceptable line when dealing with the villains she fought, and this seems to be a picture of just that. With our Vanessas concious trapped in the background, I wouldn&#39;t be surprised if we see more art related to the &quot;purging of Dark Visionary&quot; in the future (or at least I hope to see it!)As my final note, I think there is more than enough evidence to back up the theory that Heartbreaker is Tony Torus that BraithWhite posed a long while ago. The more we see of him, the more signs point to this being correct.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

I hadn&#39;t considered the flip between Guise and Wager Master, that makes Paragon of Sentience even more important if we can draw a strong connection between Scholar and the Cosmic Entity.

&nbsp;

On Ammit and Nightmist... I don&#39;t know if I agree that Mist Storm is Nightmist. It never seemed a terribly compelling arguement to me, and now that we have Darkwatch Nightmist&#39;s bio I think her story might be seperate. Darkwatch Nightmist is an Eldritch being of Magic, when she was human she got trapped in a different dimension and did the whole &quot;10,000 years in a blink of an eye&quot; struggle to get back to Earth and not fall prey to other powerful magical spirits. Sure in that way that she &quot;is the Mists&quot; now it could make sense, but only if she completely lost control, which after what she went thru seems very unlikely.

&nbsp;

However, I think I have another answer to why she is not in Tactics yet (I feel good saying she will be in it at some point). Bugbear&#39;s incap seems to show a connection between Nightmist and Bugbear, and his story seems to hint that he sought her out for help curing him. She wasn&#39;t able to, and couldn&#39;t devote time to saving him with the world falling apart around their ears with Progeny and whatever comes afterward. What if after the final battle she devotes herself to study to find a cure? Or, perhaps working on strengthening Earth&#39;s mystical defenses (in case Scholar and Guise goes down and leylines crumble). If she has secluded herself and is working solo on something only she can do (or that she thinks she can only do since Faye seems to have that sort of lone ranger mentality) then it makes since she is no longer with Dark Watch, who is more concerned with helping take care of Broken City. Actually, Nightmist might have moved on from Mystic Detective to Sorcerer Supreme and instead works more closely with the Prime Wardens (many of whom are conspicously absent and might be a clue that something else big is still going on in the world that is requiring their attention).

&nbsp;

Also supporting Heartbreaker is Tony Taurus, especially since the Tribunal shows that Heartbreaker is most likely responsible for the death of Tremata, if Tremata (an ally in Rook City) is dead, then we have to wonder what happens to the other doomed ally, and man does Tony and Heartbreaker seem to fit so well together
